From c0ee05ada9268a441e908cad0436d71b2125d800 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:24:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gbm: the lines between the two eyes of 3D frame packing are
 made black before each frame goes out

In an HDMI 3D frame packing mode the frame is the left eye, the active
space and the right eye: the 3D mode of WinSystemGbm.cpp has iHeight
with the iBlanking lines of the active space, and CGraphicContext draws
the right eye iHeight + iBlanking lines down (StereoCorrection()). Each
eye is cleared and drawn under a scissor of its own (SetStereoView(),
CRenderSystemGLES::SetViewPort()), and nothing draws the lines of the
active space: they kept what the buffer had, the two or three buffers
of the window in turn, or Kodi's own (COwnScanout), and the display was
sent whatever was left there between the eyes. PresentRender() cleared
nothing.

They are now cleared to opaque black, the colour of Kodi's own
background, after the frame is drawn and before it is swapped, in the
framebuffer that is bound, in the ordinary way and in the frame of the
GUI that a held change of mode sends alone (StereoGap.h). The scissor
box and test, the clear colour and the colour mask are left as they
were. The lines are those that CGraphicContext leaves between the eyes
(GetResInfo(): the iBlanking that it keeps for a mode with its layout in
its flags), counted against the height that the renderer draws in; the
columns of eyes side by side the same way, though no mode of Hades has
any. kodi.log says it once for each layout. Nothing changes in 2D, nor
for 3D half layouts, which have no blanking.

Kodi's own buffers are not used in a frame-packed mode of nvidia-drm
(FramePackedBufferDemands()); with i915 and amdgpu they can be (video of
more than 8 bits, OwnScanoutWanted(), and they follow the window into a
new mode), and the lines are cleared in them too. Native Dolby Vision
never takes a 3D picture, and its frames are not touched.

Not tried on hardware: no display of the tests has 3D.

The idea of clearing the active space before the swap is CroqueMr's
(libreelec-x86-DV, preview/rc4-update3, 43e1b14e7c, "Clear HDMI
frame-packing active space before swapping"); written for this tree.
